Description:
    Wires one parent→child edge of a nested form onto a resource that
    hibiki:rails:scaffold_controller already generated: the child's
    ReactiveForm, a _<child>_fields partial with path-addressed inputs
    (riding the generic Hibiki::Rails::NestedActions channel actions),
    reactive_nested on the parent form, model wiring (has_many +
    accepts_nested_attributes_for allow_destroy), the classic fields_for
    fallback in the full-page form, and the controller's params.expect
    double-array group.

    Parent and Child models must exist and be migrated, and Child must
    declare belongs_to :<parent>. An optional field list narrows or orders
    the child's form fields; the facts stay the schema's.

    Depth is composition: run once per edge. A run whose Parent is itself a
    nested child (its _<parent>_fields partial exists) nests into that
    partial instead of the row form.

    Ordering: a `position` column on the child (or --position=COLUMN) makes
    the fieldset ordered — the has_many gains an order scope, the parent
    form stamps positions from array order, and rows get ↑/↓ buttons. The
    named column is added by migration when missing; --skip-position opts
    out entirely.

Examples:
    bin/rails g hibiki:rails:nested Song Credit

    bin/rails g hibiki:rails:nested Credit Contribution

    bin/rails g hibiki:rails:nested Song Credit artist:references role:string --position=rank
